# Pairs with CloseHeadMonotone. A close overwrites the heads earlier closes recorded
# instead of max-merging with them, so a later window's close, whose own stamped
# appends all lie below a lower head, lowers the heads the marker requires and
# releases an owner an earlier close still holds. Production max-merges in
# HandOffMarkerCore.RequiredHead. Three windows are needed for the lower head to
# be choosable: the walk goes on unstamped only after a close has rejected it.
MODULE: CloseHeadMonotoneCloseOverwritesHeads
TARGET: CloseHeadMonotone
CLASS: Action
SUMMARY: a close overwrites the marker's heads rather than max-merging them
PERTURBS: Close
BOUNDS: MaxWindows = 3, MaxEpoch = 4

--- FIND
    /\ \E h \in CloseHeads : hoClosedAt' = Max2(hoClosedAt, h)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the close overwrites the recorded heads.
    /\ \E h \in CloseHeads : hoClosedAt' = h
--- END
